            <ArticleTitle>Congenital coronary aneurysm resulting in myocardial infarction: MR imaging findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>937-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 33-year-old Caucasian male who presented with myocardial infarction and a right atrial mass. Coronary catheterization demonstrated a right coronary aneurysm. In this report, we describe magnetic resonance (MR) imaging findings of a right coronary artery aneurysm with thromboembolism formation, resulting in inferior myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
